 22.9-21.5Q22.8-20.7 22.8-20.2L22.8-20.2Q22.8-17.7 23.7-16.0Q24.6-14.2 26.5-13.3Q28.4-12.3 31.4-12.3L31.4-12.3Q34.7-12.3 37.1-13.3Q39.5-14.2 41.1-16.3Q42.6-18.3 43.2-21.5L43.2-21.5L61.7-21.5Q60.3-13.5 55.7-8.5Q51-3.4 44.2-1.1Q37.4 1.2 29.6 1.2ZM81.3 1.3L81.3 1.3Q75.8 1.3 72.2-0.4Q68.6-2.1 66.9-5.3Q65.1-8.4 65.1-12.9L65.1-12.9Q65.1-14.3 65.3-15.7Q65.4-17 65.6-18.5L65.6-18.5L71.6-52.7L91.5-52.7L85.9-20.9Q85.8-20.4 85.8-20.0Q85.7-19.5 85.7-19L85.7-19Q85.7-17.3 86.4-16.1Q87-14.8 88.3-14.1Q89.5-13.4 91.3-13.4L91.3-13.4Q93.2-13.4 94.8-14.1Q96.5-14.7 97.8-15.9Q99-17 99.9-18.5Q100.7-20 101-21.7L101-21.7L106.5-52.7L126.4-52.7L117.1 0.1L100.9 0.1L100.9-7.9L100.2-7.9Q97.7-4.8 94.7-2.8Q91.6-0.7 88.3 0.3Q84.9 1.3 81.3 1.3ZM143.7 0L123.8 0L133.1-52.8L149.3-52.8L149.3-44.8L150-44.8Q151.8-47.8 154.3-49.9Q156.7-52 159.6-53.1Q162.4-54.1 165.4-54.1L165.4-54.1Q167.4-54.1 168.9-53.7Q170.4-53.3 171.1-52.9L171.1-52.9L168.2-36.2L161.8-36.2Q158.6-36.2 156.2-35.4Q153.8-34.5 152.1-32.9Q150.4-31.2 149.4-28.9Q148.3-26.5 147.8-23.5L147.8-23.5L143.7 0ZM182.8 1.2L182.8 1.2Q176.6 1.2 172.2-1.1Q167.7-3.4 165.4-7.9Q163.1-12.3 163.1-18.8L163.1-18.8Q163.1-20.7 163.3-22.9Q163.4-25 163.8-27.3L163.8-27.3Q165.4-36.3 168.9-42.2Q172.3-48.1 177.5-51.1Q182.6-54 189.1-54L189.1-54Q192.6-54 195.4-53.2Q198.2-52.4 200.4-50.7Q202.6-49 204.4-46.1L204.4-46.1L205.1-46.1L209.7-52.8L225.4-52.8L223-40Q222.4-36.8 221.8-33.4Q221.1-29.9 220.6-26.7Q220-23.5 219.5-20.8Q219-18.1 218.8-16.4Q218.5-14.6 218.5-14.1L218.5-14.1Q218.5-12.7 219.2-12.1Q219.9-11.4 221-11.4L221-11.4L223.9-11.4L222-0.8Q219.7 0.1 217.1 0.7Q214.4 1.2 211.9 1.2L211.9 1.2Q208.7 1.2 206.2 0.5Q203.6-0.2 201.9-1.8L201.9-1.8Q201-2.6 200.5-3.8Q199.9-5 199.5-6.4L199.5-6.4L198.8-6.4Q195.6-2.8 191.4-0.8Q187.1 1.2 182.8 1.2ZM190-13.5L190-13.5Q192.3-13.5 194.2-14.4Q196-15.3 197.4-16.9Q198.7-18.4 199.6-20.5Q200.4-22.5 200.8-24.8L200.8-24.8Q201.2-27 201.4-28.3Q201.6-29.5 201.7-30.2Q201.7-30.9 201.7-31.4L201.7-31.4Q201.7-33.7 201.0-35.5Q200.2-37.3 198.7-38.3Q197.1-39.3 194.6-39.3L194.6-39.3Q191.5-39.3 189.4-38.1Q187.3-36.8 186.1-34.5Q184.8-32.2 184.2-29.1L184.2-29.1Q183.6-25.9 183.3-24.3Q183-22.6 183.0-21.9Q182.9-21.1 182.9-20.6L182.9-20.6Q182.9-17.3 184.6-15.4Q186.2-13.5 190-13.5Z" fill="url(#sxlW)"/></g></svg><span>Reviewed October 29, 2026 · nclexsim.com/study-guides/copd-vs-asthma</span></div><div class="gpx-band"><p class="gpx-k">Free NCLEX-RN med-surg visual sheet</p><p class="gpx-h">COPD vs. Asthma</p><p class="gpx-l"><b>Asthma comes and goes and reverses. COPD stays and slowly gets worse.</b> Both narrow the airways.</p><div class="gkey gkp"><p class="gkey-t">Key takeaways</p><ol><li><span>Asthma reverses. COPD doesn't fully reverse and slowly worsens.</span></li><li><span>SpO₂ target <b>88–92%</b> in COPD clients at risk of CO₂ retention.</span></li><li><span>A <b>quiet chest</b> in asthma is an emergency.</span></li></ol></div></div></header></div><div class="vsheet" style="--t:#2b6c8f;--z:1.16">
<section class="hero w"><h1>COPD vs. Asthma</h1><p class="lead"><b>Asthma comes and goes and reverses. COPD stays and slowly gets worse.</b> Both narrow the airways.</p><p class="gmeta">Free · 1 printable page · Reviewed October 29, 2026</p>
<div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/guides/copd-vs-asthma.pdf" download><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v11M7 10l5 5 5-5M5 20h14"/></svg> Download the PDF</a><button class="btn alt gnp" type="button" onclick="window.print()">Print this page</button></div></section>
<div class="w"><div class="gkey gks"><p class="gkey-t">Key takeaways</p><ol><li><span>Asthma reverses. COPD doesn't fully reverse and slowly worsens.</span></li><li><span>SpO₂ target <b>88–92%</b> in COPD clients at risk of CO₂ retention.</span></li><li><span>A <b>quiet chest</b> in asthma is an emergency.</span></li></ol></div>
<div class="vvs"><div class="vc" style="--c:#2b6c8f"><p class="vch"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v8M12 12c-1.5 0-3-1-3-3M12 12c1.5 0 3-1 3-3"/><path d="M9 8C6 8 4 13 4 17c0 2 1.5 3 3 3s2-1 2-3V8zM15 8c3 0 5 5 5 9 0 2-1.5 3-3 3s-2-1-2-3V8z"/></svg><span>Asthma</span></p><div class="vcb"><ul class="vl"><li>Airway inflammation and spasm that <b>reverses</b></li><li>Comes in episodes, set off by triggers: allergens, exercise, cold air, smoke, infections</li><li>Wheeze, chest tightness, cough (often at night)</li><li>Any age; often starts young</li></ul></div></div><span class="vsx" aria-hidden="true">vs</span><div class="vc" style="--c:#5a3d6b"><p class="vch"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v8M12 12c-1.5 0-3-1-3-3M12 12c1.5 0 3-1 3-3"/><path d="M9 8C6 8 4 13 4 17c0 2 1.5 3 3 3s2-1 2-3V8zM15 8c3 0 5 5 5 9 0 2-1.5 3-3 3s-2-1-2-3V8z"/></svg><span>COPD</span></p><div class="vcb"><ul class="vl"><li>Airflow limit that <b>doesn't fully reverse</b> and slowly worsens</li><li>Mostly from smoking; emphysema and chronic bronchitis</li><li>Daily cough with sputum, breathlessness, barrel chest, tripod position</li><li>Quitting smoking is the most helpful step</li></ul></div></div></div>
<div class="vrow" style="--n:2"><div class="vc" style="--c:#1f5f6b"><p class="vch"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="9" width="18" height="6" rx="3" transform="rotate(-35 12 12)"/><path d="M9.5 8.5l5 7"/></svg><span>Inhalers</span></p><div class="vcb"><div class="tw"><table class="vt"><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Examples</th><th>Key point</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>Rescue (SABA)</b></td><td>albuterol</td><td>Fast relief. Carry it everywhere</td></tr><tr><td><b>Steroid (ICS)</b></td><td>fluticasone, budesonide</td><td>Controller. Rinse mouth after to prevent thrush</td></tr><tr><td><b>Long-acting (LABA)</b></td><td>salmeterol, formoterol</td><td>Not alone in asthma; paired with a steroid</td></tr><tr><td><b>Long-acting (LAMA)</b></td><td>tiotropium</td><td>COPD maintenance. Dry mouth</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="vsm">Bronchodilator before steroid when both are due. Some asthma plans now use one steroid-formoterol inhaler for both control and relief.</p></div></div><div class="vc" style="--c:#a5622a"><p class="vch"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12.5l4.5 4.5L19 7"/></svg><span>Peak flow zones (asthma)</span></p><div class="vcb"><div class="vzone"><div class="zg"><b>Green 80–100%</b><span>of personal best: keep going</span></div><div class="zy"><b>Yellow 50–79%</b><span>caution: use the action plan</span></div><div class="zr"><b>Red below 50%</b><span>emergency: rescue inhaler and get help</span></div></div></div></div></div>
<div class="vkeys" style="--k:3"><div class="vk"><b>88–92%</b><span>SpO₂ target for COPD clients at risk of CO₂ retention</span></div><div class="vk"><b>94–98%</b><span>SpO₂ target for most other adults</span></div><div class="vk"><b>Pursed lips</b><span>Breathe in through the nose, out slowly through pursed lips</span></div></div>
<div class="valert"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l9.5 17h-19z"/><path d="M12 10v4M12 17.5v.01"/></svg><div><b>Red flags:</b> a quiet chest in asthma (too little air moving to wheeze), can't speak full sentences, drowsiness or confusion (rising CO₂), or falling SpO₂. Never withhold oxygen from a client who is hypoxic.</div></div>
<div class="gend"><h2 class="gsh">Sources</h2><ol class="gsrc"><li>Global Initiative for Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease (GOLD). Global Strategy for the Diagnosis, Management, and Prevention of COPD, 2025 report.</li><li>Global Initiative for Asthma (GINA). Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update.</li><li>O'Driscoll BR, et al. BTS guideline for oxygen use in adults in healthcare and emergency settings. Thorax. 2017;72(Suppl 1).</li><li>National Heart, Lung, and Blood Institute. Asthma action plan and peak flow zones.</li></ol>
<p class="gfine gdis">For exam study only. In clinical practice, follow your facility's policies, the prescriber's orders, and current references. Free to print and share for personal and classroom study; not for resale. NCLEX® is a registered trademark of NCSBN, which does not endorse Vexcura.</p></div>
<div class="gmore"><h2>More med-surg visual sheets</h2><div class="gcards"><div class="gcard"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 20s-7-4.4-7-10a4 4 0 0 1 7-2.6A4 4 0 0 1 19 10c0 5.6-7 10-7 10z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/heart-failure-left-vs-right">Heart failure: left vs. right</a></b></div><p>Left backs up into the lungs, right backs up into the body. Signs, the four core medicines, daily weights, and when it's an emergency.</p><div class="gl"><a href="/guides/heart-failure-left-vs-right.pdf" download>PDF</a><small>1 page</small></div></div><div class="gcard"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3s6 6.5 6 11a6 6 0 0 1-12 0c0-4.5 6-11 6-11z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/dka-vs-hhs">DKA vs. HHS, plus insulin timing</a></b></div><p>The diagnostic numbers from the 2024 consensus, the treatment order (fluids, potassium, insulin), insulin onset and peak, and the rule of 15.</p><div class="gl"><a href="/guides/dka-vs-hhs.pdf" download>PDF</a><small>1 page</small></div></div><div class="gcard"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13 3L5 13h6l-1 8 8-10h-6z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/electrolyte-imbalances">Electrolytes: K, Na, Ca, Mg</a></b></div><p>Low vs. high for the four big electrolytes: what you'll see, the ECG clues, common causes, and the first nursing actions.</p><div class="gl"><a href="/guides/electrolyte-imbalances.pdf" download>PDF</a><small>1 page</small></div></div><div class="gcard"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 4v8M12 12c-1.5 0-3-1-3-3M12 12c1.5 0 3-1 3-3"/><path d="M9 8C6 8 4 13 4 17c0 2 1.5 3 3 3s2-1 2-3V8zM15 8c3 0 5 5 5 9 0 2-1.5 3-3 3s-2-1-2-3V8z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/abg-interpretation">ABGs in 3 steps</a></b></div><p>Read any blood gas in three steps with ROME, see the four disorders and their common causes, and check yourself with two worked examples.</p><div class="gl"><a href="/guides/abg-interpretation.pdf" download>PDF</a><small>1 page</small></div></div><div class="gcard"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l9.5 17h-19z"/><path d="M12 10v4M12 17.5v.01"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/types-of-shock">Shock: the 4 types</a></b></div><p>Hypovolemic, cardiogenic, distributive, and obstructive shock side by side, the numbers to watch, and the sepsis first-hour steps.</p><div class="gl"><a href="/guides/types-of-shock.pdf" download>PDF</a><small>1 page</small></div></div><div class="gcard"><div class="gh"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 4a3 3 0 0 0-3 3 3 3 0 0 0-2 5 3 3 0 0 0 2 5 3 3 0 0 0 3 3V4zM15 4a3 3 0 0 1 3 3 3 3 0 0 1 2 5 3 3 0 0 1-2 5 3 3 0 0 1-3 3V4z"/></svg><b><a href="/study-guides/stroke-be-fast">Stroke: BE-FAST and first-hour care</a></b></div><p>Spot it with BE-FAST, tell ischemic from hemorrhagic, the first-hour checklist with BP limits, and left- vs right-brain deficits.</p><div class="gl"><a href="/guides/stroke-be-fast.pdf" download>PDF</a><small>1 page</small></div></div></div><p><a href="/nclex-study-guides">See all free study guides</a></p></div></div></div><section class="band vxs-band"><div class="vxs-bg" data-vxs-i="0" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="vxs-sh" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="w"><h2>Bring Vexcura to your nursing program</h2><p>1,220 cited NCLEX-RN questions, adaptive practice exams, 8 NGN case studies, an Epic-style academic EHR and a clinical instructor workspace. The school pays; students and instructors are always free, and every plan includes everything. Students: ask your instructor, or join with your school's code.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/for-nursing-schools">See Vexcura for nursing schools</a><a class="btn alt" href="/for-nursing-schools#pricing">Pricing</a><a class="btn alt" href="/#signup">Join with a school code</a></div></div></section></main><footer class="foot"><div class="w"><div class="cols">
   <div><p class="fh">Vexcura</p><p>NCLEX-RN prep and an Epic-style academic EHR, licensed to nursing schools and facilities. Free for students and instructors. Built by a registered nurse.</p></div>
